# Machine-written files: these change without anyone editing them, so their
# worktree copy drifts from whatever git has committed. That is the class that
# turned a brownout into unrecoverable object-DB loss on 2026-07-30 — a lost
# blob for a source file can always be restored from disk with
# `git hash-object -w`, but not one whose content has since been rewritten.
# Keep them untracked so a power cut can only ever cost recoverable data.
*.log.*
logs/
*.jsonl
kiki_speeches/

# Downloaded toolchains/archives — refetchable, and a 62MB blob makes every
# `git gc` repack a long window of writing on an SD card.
/go*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz
